{"raw": {"https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0239&BRID=364393&lang=1": {"title": "Coordinator, Academic Communications, Faculty of Science", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Coordinator, Academic Communications, Faculty of Science Office of the Dean Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: October 22, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0239 Status: Temporary Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 7 Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $31.33 - $37.43/Hour Position Description Job Summary The Academic Communications Coordinator is actively involved in engaging with external stakeholders and incorporating community input to develop and adjust programs within the faculty area. Additionally, they build and maintain relationships with external stakeholders to expand education opportunities and identify potential partnerships with community organizations. The Coordinator supports the Dean\u2019s office on agreements and partnerships, and provides administrative support to Faculty Council and various subcommittees. This position is responsible for maintaining the faculty area\u2019s website and social media accounts, creating promotional materials for events, and coordinating event planning from concept to completion. Qualifications Bachelor's degree from a recognized post-secondary institution. Minimum of two (2) years related experience in a post-secondary institution, or similar organization. Excellent written and oral communication skills, including website writing, editing and marketing and promotions. Strong problem solving and critical thinking skills. Demonstrated professionalism and ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to remain calm under pressure. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work creatively and effectively as a member of a team. Proven success in developing and maintain positive working relationships with internal and external partners. Experience in agenda preparations, note-taking, transcription and follow-up for large meetings. Event planning experience is preferred. Knowledge of Microsoft Office Knowledge of editing and maintaining website content. How To Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0045&BRID=364230&lang=1": {"title": "Research Assistant II (Peace and Reconciliation Centre)", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Research Assistant II (Peace and Reconciliation Centre) Research & Graduate Studies Chilliwack (CEP) Application deadline: October 21, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0045 Status: Temporary Contract Term: Nov 2026 - March 2027 Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 8 Hours/Week: 14 Salary: $35.14 - $41.91/Hour Position Description Job Summary The Research Assistant II works under the supervision of the Director, Peace and Reconciliation Centre (PARC), and supports community-engaged research, educational programming, knowledge mobilization, and reconciliation initiatives associated with the St\u00f3:lo Peoples. The incumbent performs advanced research, project coordination, stakeholder engagement, facilitation, evaluation, and administrative functions in support of project objectives. The incumbent works collaboratively with Indigenous communities, St\u00f3:lo partners, researchers, students, and project stakeholders. The incumbent exercises cultural sensitivity, discretion, and sound judgement when working with Indigenous communities and research participants and provides project-specific guidance and support to students, volunteers, and other project personnel. Qualifications Undergraduate degree in Indigenous Studies, History, Anthropology, Sociology, Criminology, Political Science, Education, Social Work, Geography, Peace and Conflict Studies, Communications, or another relevant discipline from a recognized postsecondary institution. Demonstrated knowledge of Indigenous histories, reconciliation, decolonization, cultural humility, or community-engaged research. Minimum of two (2) years related experience supporting research, community-engaged projects, educational initiatives, or reconciliation-related work. Demonstrated knowledge of Indigenous histories, reconciliation, decolonization, cultural humility, or community-engaged research. Experience conducting interviews, focus groups, community consultations, or stakeholder engagement activities. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications including Word, Excel, Outlook PowerPoint, Teams, and related technologies. Strong research, analytical, and writing skills, and experience preparing reports and knowledge mobilization materials. Demonstrated experience with working respectfully with Indigenous communities and organizations. Strong research, analytical, and writing skills, including experience preparing reports and knowledge mobilization materials. Experience conducting interviews, focus groups, community consultations, or stakeholder engagement activities. Experience using qualitative and/or quantitative research methods and software. Ability to work independently under minimal supervision, exercising good judgement and initiative. Excellent interpersonal, facilitation, and communication skills. Demonstrated organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to deal sensitively, effectively, and professionally with students, staff, faculty and research participants. Ability to handle sensitive information in a confidential and professional manner. Well-developed interpersonal skills and written and oral communication skills. Strong reviewing, proofreading, editing, and formatting skills. Ability to learn and apply sound research techniques, methodology and logical critical analysis. Experience organizing and supporting research meetings, events and activities is required. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and/ or weekends as required. Ability to travel to off-site locations as required. Access to reliable transportation may be required for off-site field work. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0926-1003&BRID=364387&lang=1": {"title": "Analyst II, Systems (Applications)", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Analyst II, Systems (Applications) IT Services - Applications Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: October 22, 2026 Job Number: J0926-1003 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: IT Professional Salary Schedule, Group 4 Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $89,203.20 - $106,854.07/Year Position Description Job Summary The Analyst II, Systems is responsible for complex troubleshooting and problem solving of systems used by students, staff and faculty across the University. The Analyst II, Systems responds to complex technical issues and actively participates in the development of long-term business application and enterprise (ERP) system projects. The incumbent values both team success and individual achievement and champions a culture of continuous improvement. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s Degree in computer science or a related field. Minimum of six (6) years of experience in programming and integrating applications; preferably in a web environment. Familiarity to business/enterprise applications such as, Ellucian Banner, Blackboard, Infosilem and Transact is an asset, HTML, CSS, Groovy/Java, PHP, Python, Javascript and automation scripting is required. Ability to provide technical assistance and advice to peers and the user community Knowledge of database principals and APIs (Application Programming Interfaces). Demonstrated knowledge and use of Oracle SQL, PLSQL , Microsoft SQL and LDAP /Active Directory. Experience in project management is an asset. Experience designing, building, install, configuring and supporting applications on Linux and Windows Operating Systems. Ability to work effectively as a member of a team. Ability to proactively provide communication and customer service to users, vendors, and other key stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to continuous learning and professional development. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0113&BRID=364055&lang=1": {"title": "Sessional Instructor, Planning, Geography & Environmental Studies", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Sessional Instructor, Planning, Geography & Environmental Studies Planning, Geography & Environmental Studies Abbotsford (Clearbrook) Application deadline: October 20, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0113 Status: Sessional Open Positions: 2 Salary Schedule: Sessional Salary Schedule, Group B Hours/Week: 6 Salary: $9,213.32 - $9,428.83/Section Job Summary The Department of Planning, Geography and Environmental Studies (PGES) creates collaborative opportunities for students and community organizations to explore the geography of natural and human environments and plan a resilient future. PGES offers Majors in BA Geography, Community & Regional Planning, Environmental Studies and an Associate Certificate in Applied GIS. The Department requires sessional faculty for the Winter 2027 semester and beyond to teach the following two courses: GEOG 318: Water Resources Management This course examines the issues surrounding water as a global resource and the scientific principles involved in water resources management. Emphasis is placed on the understanding of the role that water as a resource has within our societies, including our perception of water as a resource, contamination of water, treatment of water, and possible impacts on water supply resulting from climate change. Field trips outside of class time may be required. Please refer to department website for field trip scheduling information. Detailed course outline for the aforementioned course is available at: https://www.ufv.ca/calendar/CourseOutlines/PDFs/GEOG/ PLAN 410: Indigenizing Planning: Indigenous Land Use and Community Planning Examine ways colonization and colonialism in urban and community planning influenced Indigenous peoples\u2019 connection to the environment, socioeconomics, culture, and cultural practices. Through the lens of reconciliation, cultural humility, and cultural awareness, students consider the strength and resilience of the Indigenous nations in continuing to address environmental, socio- economic, and political issues through the context of land use, environmental stewardship, and cultural identify Detailed course outline for the aforementioned course is available at: https://www.ufv.ca/calendar/CourseOutlines/PDFs/PLAN/ Qualifications Applicants must possess at minimum a Master of Arts degree in geography, environmental studies, planning or a closely related field. Applicants must be able to demonstrate proficiency in the subject area and teaching excellence (or the potential for teaching excellence). Preferred criteria include previous post-secondary teaching experience. We are seeking a collegial, energetic, and innovative individual to effectively mentor students from a diverse range of backgrounds and abilities. How to Apply Interested candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, copies of all recent teaching evaluations (if applicable), and the names of three referees. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at candidate.njoynhelp@cgi.com or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Incase of questions/queries please contact: afia.raja@ufv.ca (Department Head, Planning, Geography and Environmental Studies, UFV) About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0926-0727&BRID=363947&lang=1": {"title": "Assistant, Groundskeeper", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Assistant, Groundskeeper Campus Planning & Facilities Management Abbotsford (King Road) Chilliwack (CEP) Application deadline: October 19, 2026 Job Number: J0926-0727 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 3 Hours/Week: 17.5 Salary: $24.62 - $29.40/Hour Position Description Job Summary The Groundskeeper Assistant provides detailed grounds keeping services to UFV, maintaining the general appearance, cleanliness and safety of campus grounds, parking lots, entrances, walkways and patios. Key responsibilities include seasonal maintenance of the existing grounds and landscaping on the Abbotsford and Chilliwack campuses by operating hand and powered tools and equipment. Tasks primarily include litter pick up, garden maintenance (watering, weeding, mulching), lawn maintenance, power blowing, pruning, shearing, edging, tree debris cleanup, and snow removal. This role ensures that grounds are pleasant, both visually and operatively, at all times. Qualifications Certificate in Landscape Horticulture required from a recognized institution preferred. One (1) year commercial gardening experience, grounds keeping, and/or green industry, preferably at a large institution. Valid BC Drivers License, and own (or have access to) a vehicle. Strong aptitude for landscape maintenance, soft landscape construction and/or ecology. First Aid training desirable. Strong time management skills with the ability to prioritize tasks appropriately. The ability to direct and follow a set work schedule with minimum direction required. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0926-0603&BRID=363808&lang=1": {"title": "Officer, Operations & Stewardship", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Officer, Operations & Stewardship Relationship and Fund Development Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: November 1, 2026 Job Number: J0926-0603 Status: Temporary Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 7 Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $57,137.65 - $68,268.36/Year Position Description Job Summary The Officer, Operations and Stewardship provides operational support to the Relationship and Fund Development team through the coordination of fundraising administration, donor stewardship, gift processing, advancement systems, communications, and operational activities that support the University's fundraising priorities. The position is responsible for administering gift processing, maintaining the integrity of donor information within Raiser's Edge NXT (RE NXT), coordinating fundraising operations, preparing reports and donor communications, supporting stewardship initiatives, and providing operational and logistical support for fundraising activities and events. Working collaboratively with internal departments and external stakeholders, the incumbent contributes to the efficient delivery of fundraising services and positive donor experiences. As a front-line representative of Relationship and Fund Development, the Officer responds to donor, alumni, and community inquiries, provides professional customer service, and supports donor engagement through responsive communication and effective operational coordination. Qualifications Diploma in Business Administration, Office Administration, Fundraising Management, Public Administration, Philanthropy, or another related discipline from a recognized post-secondary institution. An equivalent combination of education and directly related advancement operations or fundraising administration experience may be considered. A bachelor's degree is considered an asset. Minimum three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in advancement operations, fundraising administration, donor information management, donor stewardship, gift administration, or a comparable advancement, alumni relations, or development environment, preferably within a post-secondary institution or not-for-profit organization. Demonstrated experience using Raiser's Edge NXT or a comparable fundraising CRM/database. Experience supporting gift administration, donor stewardship, financial processes, and data management. Demonstrated intermediate to advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, Teams, and reporting tools. Experience with fundraising communications, email marketing platforms, event management systems, or online giving platforms is an asset. Experience using project management software such as Wrike an asset. Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to communicate clearly, professionally, and diplomatically by telephone, email, and in person with donors, alumni, volunteers, senior university leaders, and community members. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and attention-to-detail skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining accuracy and confidentiality. Demonstrated experience providing professional customer service in a role requiring frequent verbal communication and relationship management. Demonstrated ability to actively listen, accurately interpret verbal instructions and stakeholder requests, and communicate information clearly and accurately with minimal supervision. Demonstrated ability to prepare, edit, and proofread correspondence while ensuring accuracy, clarity, tone, and consistency. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment when responding to inquiries and representing the University. Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to build productive relationships across the University and with external partners. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a collaborative team environment. Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, accessibility, Indigenization, and reconciliation. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0626-1023&BRID=363916&lang=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Planning, Geography, and Environmental Studies", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Assistant Professor, Planning, Geography, and Environmental Studies Planning, Geography & Environmental Studies Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: January 29, 2027 Job Number: J0626-1023 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Teaching Faculty Salary Schedule Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $70,437.00 - $112,872.00/Year Job Summary UFV's Department of Planning, Geography and Environmental Studies (PGES) in the Faculty of Science invites applications for a tenure-track, open-rank Professor of Land-Use Planning with an interest in one or more of the following areas: sustainable development, food security, environmental, and Indigenous community planning. The successful applicant will join a thriving faculty that supports programs in Geography, Environmental Studies, and Geographic Information Systems (GIS). The Bachelor of Regional and Community Planning (BRCP) degree has recently been accredited and has strong enrollment. The successful candidate will help to further grow and strengthen the new planning program in PGES and contribute to practicums and professional experience, PGES programs\u2019 curriculum development and teaching. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses and supervise undergraduate research students through studio, applied practicum, and independent study courses. Teaching assignments may include Settlements(PLAN 160), Social Geography: The Urban Experience (GEOG 241), GIS for the Built Environment (GEOG 355), Quantitative Methods in Geography (GEOG 252), Planning Law (PLAN 310) and Indigenous Land Use and Community Planning (PLAN 410), but the final list will be tailored to the expertise of the successful candidate. In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will actively participate in PGES activities, service, events, and initiatives, and will be committed to ongoing professional development. PGES seeks a collegial and energetic individual with exceptional communication skills, demonstrated excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level, and experience in teaching across traditional disciplinary boundaries and delivering courses in community settings. The successful candidate is expected to build relationships with Fraser Valley municipalities and Indigenous communities by providing students with collaborative and integrative applied experiential learning opportunities. Incorporating Indigenous perspectives in the curriculum is essential, as is teaching international students and managing the needs of students in a diverse learning environment. Short-listed applicants will have an emerging record of applied research or professional productivity commensurate with their experience. The ability to attract external funding and establish a successful applied research program at UFV to support research and student learning experiences are highly desirable. The ability to use Geographic Information Systems (GIS), Remote Sensing, statistical software (SPSS/STATA), and emerging technologies such as Artificial Intelligence to support land-use planning will be an asset, as is experience with community outreach in agricultural regions with rapidly growing urban centers. Qualifications Extensive knowledge of land-use planning: urban spatial structure and physical design within urban and regional settings. A master\u2019s degree in urban and regional planning or a closely related field from a recognized post-secondary institution is required, in addition to extensive professional experience. However, a PhD in the mentioned disciplines is preferred. Registered Professional Planner certification with the Canadian Institute of Planners, facilitated by the Planning Standards Board of Canada, is required . Teaching experience at the undergraduate level with recent evidence of teaching excellence is preferred. Familiarity with technology-supported teaching both in the classroom, online and in the planning profession. Effective cross-cultural, interdisciplinary communication skills and experience working with Indigenous communities are assets. A growing list of impactful applied research and/or community-based planning initiatives. Interest in service contribution to PGES, UFV, and Indigenous communities of the Fraser Valley. How to Apply To be considered for this position, please submit a complete application package that includes a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy statement, research interest statement, samples of scholarly activities (e.g., publication or project portfolio), and three letters of reference. In your application, please indicate your eligibility to work legally in Canada. Applications will be reviewed by the SAC in December 2026, however the posting will be kept open for applications until the end of January 2027. You will receive a confirmation email once you successfully apply for the position. If not, do not hesitate to contact the Njoyn Help Desk at candidate.njoynhelp@cgi.com or 1-877-427-7717, Monday to Friday, 8 a.m. to 8 p.m. (EST). UFV is committed to equity in employment, and all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and a verification of their education credentials. For further information about the position, please contact Dr. Cherie Enns, RPP, Chair, Bachelor of Regional and Community Planning, University of the Fraser Valley, at cherie.enns@ufv.ca. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0726-1025&BRID=363775&lang=1": {"title": "Senior Research Analyst, Institutional Research & Integrated Planning", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Senior Research Analyst, Institutional Research & Integrated Planning Institutional Research & Planning Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: October 22, 2026 Job Number: J0726-1025 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 11 Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $75,688.84 - $88,423.98/Year Position Description Job Summary The Senior Research Analyst collects, develops, analyzes, and communicates institutional data and other information to constituents throughout the university, to support and enhance decision making, problem solving, strategic planning, policy development, and institutional self-assessment. The incumbent conducts and manages the design, implementation, and analysis of quantitative and qualitative research for both internal and external parties. The Senior Research Analyst prepares data, analysis, narrative, and presents results. The incumbent assists in the creation of Business Intelligence reports and dashboards. The position assumes a senior role in regular and customized reporting, providing training, guidance, and structure to junior staff as necessary, in conjunction with the AVP. The Senior Research Analyst brings forward proposals for new projects and leads, designs, and conducts all levels of research projects in the department. Qualifications Minimum of a bachelor\u2019s degree in a relevant field required from a recognized, post-secondary institution. A post baccalaureate certificate in data analysis or equivalent is also required. A graduate degree in a relevant field is considered an asset. Minimum of five (5) years\u2019 relevant experience, preferably in a higher education setting. Skill in data analysis, statistical software applications, and social science and business research methodologies. Experience in Advanced statistical, analytical and computer programming, preferably within higher education data systems and higher education topics. Ability to formulate and advance research projects. Ability to lead others in projects. Demonstrated experience in the successful management of multiple and short-term and long-term projects, independent completion of projects. Excellent verbal, written, numerical, and graphical communication skills. Demonstrated success in working collegially with administrators, faculty, staff, and students. Extensive experience with complex data sets including manipulating, merging, restructuring and analyzing large data sets. High capacity for accuracy and detail. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0726-0709&BRID=358195&lang=1": {"title": "Sessional Instructor, School of Health Studies", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Sessional Instructor, School of Health Studies Office of the Dean Chilliwack (CEP) Job Number: J0726-0709 Status: Sessional Open Positions: 9 Salary Schedule: Sessional Salary Schedule, Group A Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $8,104.04 - $8,319.55/Section Job Summary The School of Health Studies, part of the Faculty of Health Sciences, offers a range of nursing program options that create exciting opportunities for teaching and academic engagement. The Faculty is recognized for delivering high-quality educational experiences and producing graduates who are in high demand. Located on a technologically advanced campus within the Canada Education Park, the School of Health Studies fosters innovation in teaching and provides access to cutting-edge simulation learning environments. The School of Health Studies requires temporary/sessional faculty to teach in the following program areas: Bachelor of Science in Nursing program: The BSN program offers a four-year program stream and a 2.5 year LPN Access to BSN stream. The BSN program requires part-time/sessional faculty for clinical instruction in the areas of gerontology, medical-surgical, home health, mental health, public health, pediatrics, and child-bearing families. Successful candidates will hold a Baccalaureate degree in nursing and have a strong related clinical practice foundation. A master\u2019s degree is preferred. Practical Nursing program: The PN program requires part-time/sessional faculty for clinical instruction in gerontological, medical and surgical practice settings. Successful candidates will hold a Baccalaureate degree in nursing and a strong related clinical practice foundation. Candidates with a diploma in nursing with extensive clinical practice experience will be considered. Health Care Assistant program: The HCA program requires part-time/sessional faculty for instruction in gerontological practice settings. Successful candidates will hold a Baccalaureate degree in nursing and a strong related clinical practice foundation. Candidates with a diploma in nursing with extensive clinical practice experience will be considered. NOTE: Current BCCNM registration in good standing without limits or conditions, or eligibility for registration with BCCNM prior to start of sessional faculty position is a requirement. How to Apply Please submit the required documents through the online application portal: Cover letter with the program of interest clearly indicated Resume/CV About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0926-0867&BRID=364716&lang=1": {"title": "Maintenance Technician", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Maintenance Technician Campus Planning & Facilities Management Application deadline: October 27, 2026 Job Number: J0926-0867 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Anticipated Start Date: 26/10/2026 Campus(es): Abbotsford (King Road) Hours/Week: 35 % Full Time: 100 Total Months/Year: 12 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 7 Salary: $57,137.65 - $68,268.36/Year Position Description Job Summary The Maintenance Technician (MT) provides response to daily requests logged through the Facilities Service Desk in the capacity of both reactive and planned preventative maintenance in all areas of building operations and services. This includes mechanical, electrical, plumbing, structural, air-conditioning equipment and general service calls relating to (but not limited to): door/lock issues, minor carpentry, furniture repair/installation, painting and general building assistance. The MT works closely to oversee and manage external contractors with a technical skill to perform reactive repairs, planned preventative maintenance on equipment as well as general repairs/upgrades. The MT coordinates the timing and completion of contract services to ensure the efficiency of contracted work. The MT employs responsible and safe workplace practices in accordance with UFV and other regulatory bodies and utilizes a keen eye for detail, combined with solid technical knowledge, to support the smooth operation of university buildings and equipment. Qualifications 5th Class Power engineer certification required. Trades Qualification in relevant discipline or Certification in building systems or maintenance programs is preferred. Five (5) years of experience working with heating, air conditioning, ventilation, electrical, plumbing and associated mechanical systems, and a basic knowledge of all construction trades. Experiencing utilizing a Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS) to manage workload, including both routine and planned preventative maintenance tasks. Experience operating high-reach hydraulic lifts. Valid BC driver\u2019s license. WHMIS certification mandatory. Ability to lift 50-60 pounds. Ability to manage competing priorities and discern primary areas of focus. A working knowledge of computers and building control systems is required. Experience in the coordinating and monitoring of trades personnel and contractors is desirable. Required to work in environments exposed to toxic fumes, loud noise, dust, extreme temperatures, heights, and equipment with moving parts that requires employee to be cognizant of all safety protocols & procedures inherent in their field, making use of professional protection equipment such as ear plugs, safety glasses, respirators, and gloves. Duties require a high degree of physical exertion which includes bending down, kneeling, crouching for extended periods of time, pulling, pushing, manually carrying, lifting & transporting heavy objects. Required to work in inclement weather conditions ranging from extreme cold periods of rain, snow, ice, freezing rain, high winds, to extreme hot periods and heat waves. Ability to work on multiple campuses and on different shifts, based on operational needs. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0159&BRID=364678&lang=1": {"title": "Manager, Community Programming and Experience", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Manager, Community Programming and Experience Community Programming & Experience Application deadline: October 26, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0159 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Anticipated Start Date: 16/11/2026 Campus(es): Abbotsford (King Road) Hours/Week: 35 % Full Time: 100 Total Months/Year: 12 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 10 Salary: $71,898.38 - $84,432.96/Year Position Description Job Summary The Manager, Community Programming and Experience (CPE) provides operational leadership for the day-to-day management of the Community Programming and Experience department, ensuring the effective coordination, delivery, and continuous improvement of community engagement initiatives, signature programs, and institutional events that support the University's community engagement priorities. Reporting to the Director, the Manager oversees departmental operations, supervises staff, monitors program budgets, supports the implementation of approved risk management practices, and ensures compliance with University policies, procedures, and service standards. Through effective operational planning, resource coordination, and people leadership, the Manager supports the successful delivery of more than thirty annual and ongoing initiatives, including Convocation, Open House, National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, International Women's Day, and the Community Report and Celebration. Working closely with the Director, the Strategist, the Coordinator, and internal and external stakeholders, the Manager coordinates operational activities, monitors departmental performance, and ensures staff, resources, and administrative processes are effectively aligned to support the successful delivery of programs and events. The Manager provides operational advice, analysis, and reporting to support departmental planning and informed decision-making; monitors operational risks, budgets, and service standards; and fosters collaborative relationships that contribute to effective service delivery and positive community experiences. Through strong operational leadership and a commitment to continuous improvement, the Manager helps ensure the Community Programming and Experience department delivers high-quality, inclusive, and well-coordinated programs and services that strengthen community engagement and support the University's strategic objectives. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in a relevant field (e.g., Communications, Public Relations, Project Management, Business Administration, or related discipline) from a recognized, post-secondary institution. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in community engagement, institutional programming, event management, stakeholder relations, and project management. Demonstrated experience leading complex initiatives, supervising staff, managing budgets, and working with diverse internal and external stakeholders. Experience leading teams in a unionized environment. Experience interpreting and applying organizational policies, procedures, and administrative practices. Demonstrated ability to lead change within an operational environment and foster continuous improvement through effective planning, process improvement, and staff engagement. Strong project management skills with the ability to oversee multiple initiatives simultaneously. Excellent communication, relationship-building, and stakeholder engagement skills. Experience monitoring budgets, preparing financial information, and supporting sound financial stewardship. Experience coordinating departmental operations, allocating resources, and monitoring operational performance in a complex organizational environment. Experience mediating diverse stakeholder perspectives and facilitating collaborative decision-making. Demonstrated ability to lead operational planning and translate strategic priorities into actionable work plans. Experience supporting the implementation of organizational risk management practices and operational procedures. Demonstrated experience supervising, coaching, and developing professional staff. Proven ability to develop and manage vendor relationships, contracts, and service agreements. Strong analytical skills with experience evaluating program outcomes and implementing improvements. Demonstrated ability to represent an organization in community-facing roles with professionalism, tact, and diplomacy. Experience coordinating multi-departmental initiatives or working groups. Training or certification in project management (e.g., PMP, CAPM, Agile methodologies) is an asset. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0323&BRID=364675&lang=1": {"title": "Manager, Procurement", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Manager, Procurement Financial Services Application deadline: October 26, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0323 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Campus(es): Abbotsford (Clearbrook) Hours/Week: 35 % Full Time: 100 Total Months/Year: 12 Salary Schedule: Exempt Salary Schedule, Group 11 Salary: $94,443.00 - $138,516.00/Year Compensation Details: Compensation beyond the mid-point requires approval by the Public Sector Employers' Council Secretariat (PSEC). Position Description Job Summary The Manager, Procurement, leads and oversees the university's Procurement function, ensuring the effective, compliant, and value-driven acquisition of goods and services in support of institutional objectives. Reporting to the Director, Financial Services, the role provides leadership to the Procurement team and serves as a trusted advisor to the university community on procurement, sourcing, contracting, and supplier management matters. The Manager promotes best practices, continuous improvement, operational efficiency, and risk management while fostering strong relationships with internal stakeholders, suppliers, and external partners. This role oversees the procurement process from planning and competitive solicitation through contract administration and supplier management, ensuring the acquisition of goods and services is conducted in a fair, transparent, cost-effective, and compliant manner consistent with university policy, applicable legislation, and public sector procurement standards. Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Business Administration, Commerce, Supply Chain Management, Public Administration, or related discipline. Professional designation in supply chain or procurement management, such as SCMP (Supply Chain Management Professional), CPSM (Certified Professional in Supply Management), or equivalent designation. Minimum five (5) years of progressively responsible procurement, sourcing, and contract management experience, preferably within a public sector, broader public sector, or post-secondary environment. Demonstrated experience leading competitive procurement processes, including Requests for Proposals (RFPs), Requests for Quotations (RFQs), Invitations to Tender (ITTs), and other public procurement methodologies. Experience developing, negotiating, administering, and managing contracts and supplier agreements. Experience interpreting and applying procurement policies, trade agreements, applicable legislation, and public procurement best practices. Demonstrated ability to provide procurement guidance and support to a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders. Proven leadership experience, including managing staff and supporting the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of procurement systems, processes, and operational effectiveness. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and competing deadlines in a complex organizational environment. Experience identifying and implementing process improvements, cost-saving opportunities, and operational efficiencies while maintaining service quality and value. Strong analytical, problem-solving, negotiation, communication, and relationship management skills. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link \u2713 Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More\u2026"}, "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0726-1099&BRID=359344&lang=1": {"title": "Program Technician, Agriculture", "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Program Technician, Agriculture Agriculture Technology Application deadline: October 26, 2026 Job Number: J0726-1099 Status: Temporary Open Positions: 1 Anticipated Start Date: 08/09/2026 Contract End Date: 11/12/2026 Campus(es): Chilliwack (CEP) Hours/Week: 17.5 % Full Time: 50 Total Months/Year: 4 Indicate Month(s): Sept, Oct, Nov, Dec Contract Term: Sept 8, 2026-Dec 11, 2026 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 7 Salary: $31.33 - $37.43/Hour Position Description Job Summary Under the direction of the Agriculture department head, the relief technician will support the delivery of livestock courses over the course of the Fall 2026 semester. Duties & Responsibilities Assists instructors in delivering course specific learning outcomes by preparing supplies and materials beforehand and assisting during scheduled class time including on field trips. Maintains barn facilities including animal water supply systems, livestock feed delivery systems, livestock environmental systems, and heavy equipment. Ensures compliance of all lab equipment and procedures with all internal and external regulatory agencies such as the Animal Care Committee, Biosafety Committee and WorkSafeBC. Sets up and maintains equipment and facilities for lab experiments and demonstrations; ensures that materials, equipment and supplies are prepared and available for students and instructors use as required; maintains up-to-date inventory. Attends Agriculture Department meetings and provides updates/concerns/feedback on status of facilities, supplies, and student conduct to dept. head and faculty. Communicates in a respectful and professional manner with all members of the team, department, University community and external partners. Collaborates effectively as a team member, including sharing information, cross training and interpersonal cooperation. Demonstrates respect for all members of the UFV community, actively contributing to an environment of acceptance, accessibility and inclusivity of others. Actively engages in learning and activities related to actioning indigenization and understanding the impact of colonialism and the purpose of reconciliation. Participates in committees and project teams as required. Undertakes related duties as assigned, consistent with the job grade of the position Qualifications Diploma in Agriculture (or equivalent) from a recognized post-secondary institution. Three (3) years related experience, preferably in a commercial agriculture facility and/or post-secondary teaching environment. Must hold a valid BC Drivers License and own (or have access to) a vehicle. Licensed to operate a skidsteer with implements (forks, buckets, mowers, augers, tillers, etc) and a 3-point hitch on tractors. Training in WHMIS and workplace safety regulations is necessary. Physical fitness sufficient for moderate manual labour, and physical exertion including pushing, lifting and assisting large livestock frequently. Must be highly motivated, detail oriented, and have good organization, able to prioritize tasks and efficiently accomplish goals and objectives with minimum supervision. Basic computer proficiency required. Strong written and oral communication skills essential. Required to work in environments exposed to noxious fumes, dust, loud noise, heights, and equipment with moving parts that requires employee to be cognizant of all safety protocols & procedures inherent in their field, making use of personal protective equipment such as ear plugs, safety glasses, respirators, and gloves. Required to work in inclement weather conditions ranging from extreme cold periods of rain, snow, ice, freezing rain, high winds, to extreme hot periods and heat waves. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check. Shortlisted applicants will also be required to provide copies of their most recent evaluation summary. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'em\u00e9ylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in St\u00f3:lo T\u00e9m:\u00e9xw (St\u00f3:lo Land; St\u00f3:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the St\u00f3:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW \u2014 which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-5